## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to translate product goals into a concrete cost model that accounts for on-device constraints, security requirements, and regulatory concerns. It also probes understanding of trade-offs for multi-app isolation, update mechanics, and privacy-by-design principles.

## Key Concepts
- On-device ML model footprints and TEE (Trusted Execution Environment) architecture
- Cross-app isolation with per-app policy overrides
- Telemetry budgeting and data minimization under privacy regulations
- OTA update economics, delta patching, and cryptographic key rotation
- Compliance frameworks (GDPR, CCPA), privacy-by-design, and break-even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-break-even calculator
function needsGoNoGo(serverSavingsPerMonth, deviceCostsPerMonth, months) {
  const netSavings = serverSavingsPerMonth - deviceCostsPerMonth;
  const cumulativeSavings = netSavings * months;
  return {
    breakEvenMonths: deviceCostsPerMonth / netSavings,
    go: cumulativeSavings > 0 && months >= 18
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to translate a complex edge-ML rollout into a precise 2-year CBA, balancing hardware, cloud costs, and real-world benefits like downtime and maintenance savings.

## Key Concepts

- Edge computing and on-device training
- Federated learning and privacy implications
- CAPEX vs OPEX modeling
- Downtime reduction and MTBF uplift as financial drivers
- Handling non-IID data and drift in multi-site deployments

## Code Example

```javascript
function estimateROI(capex, opexPerMonth, savingsPerMonth, horizonMonths) {
  const totalOpex = opexPerMonth * horizonMonths;
  const totalCost = capex + totalOpex;
  const totalSavings = savingsPerMonth * horizonMonths;
  const roi = (totalSavings - totalCost) / totalCost;
  return { totalCost, totalSavings, roi };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor and mitigate model drift across sites?
- What metrics would you track to validate the ROI assumptions and trigger governance gates?

## Why This Is Asked
This question explores a privacy-preserving on-device machine learning use case with real-world constraints including energy efficiency, latency requirements, data minimization principles, and regulatory compliance. It emphasizes the importance of measurable go/no-go criteria and a concrete break-even timeline for implementation decisions.

## Key Concepts
- On-device machine learning models (autoencoder/isolation forest)
- Energy and performance budgeting for background tasks
- Data minimization and privacy impact assessments
- Go/No-Go criteria and break-even horizon analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
function detectAnomaly(readings, threshold){
  const mean = readings.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)/readings.length;
  const variance = readings.reduce((a,b)=>a+Math.pow(b-mean,2),0)/readings.length;
  return Math.abs(readings[readings.length-1] - mean) > threshold * Math.sqrt(variance);
}
```

